# Git commits

When creating commits in this repository:

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by`, `Co-Authored-By`, or any co-author trailer.
- **Never** use `git commit --trailer` (especially not for Cursor or any AI tool).
- Use only: `git commit -m "type: description"` (optional body via HEREDOC if needed).
- Follow `docs/COMMIT_MESSAGES.md`: subject line must be `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.
- Do not amend or rewrite commits to inject co-author lines.

The Husky **commit-msg** hook strips any injected `Co-authored-by` lines and rejects invalid subjects.
